<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tangata manu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Birdman cult</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tangata manu ('bird man') was the winner of a yearly competition on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a> (Easter Island), centred on the ceremonial village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orongo">Orongo</a>. Each spring men representing rival chiefs swam to the islet of Motu Nui to wait for the first sooty tern egg; the chief whose man brought it back became bird man for a year, with sacred status. The cult flourished after the age of the moai and ended in the 1860s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tangata-manu.jpg" alt="Tangata manu" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kallerna · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Easter_Island_11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
